00:06:23.320 --> 00:06:28.980
judgment on an ongoing situation. The question worth considering, how do personal factors influence

00:06:28.980 --> 00:06:34.120
high stakes foreign policy decisions? Now to really understand the story's dominating today,

00:06:34.540 --> 00:06:39.240
there is something most coverage leaves out. The Strait of Hormuz is one of the world's most

00:06:39.240 --> 00:06:44.960
critical energy choke points. Roughly 20% of global oil consumption passes through this narrow

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:52.180
waterway between Iran and Oman. When tanker traffic halts or faces new fees, the effect is not abstract.

00:06:52.980 --> 00:06:58.600
Refineries adjust purchases immediately, futures markets price in risk within hours.

00:06:59.140 --> 00:07:04.900
That risk premium appears at petrol stations within days. Governments then face higher value

00:07:04.900 --> 00:07:10.820
added tax receipts on the one hand and angry motorists on the other. What changes how you see the debate

00:07:10.820 --> 00:07:15.640
is recognizing that neither complete freedom of navigation nor full Iranian sovereignty

00:07:15.640 --> 00:07:20.240
